WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:08.980 --> 00:00:15.660
In Japanese what Maria is saying roughly translates to (see above):

00:00:19.720 --> 00:00:21.400
This double entendre actually refers

00:00:21.480 --> 00:00:24.940
to the corpse at the end of the Fishing Hamlet here.

00:00:25.420 --> 00:00:29.880
While both the English and the Japanese do imply this, the Japanese translation

00:00:30.180 --> 00:00:33.780
is way more overt about it by saying "corpse fishing".

00:00:33.940 --> 00:00:38.100
This is just one of many examples of meaning lost in translation.

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:42.400
Because when the text and dialogue in Bloodborne was translated to English

00:00:42.760 --> 00:00:45.900
certain changes would've been made by the localization team

00:00:45.900 --> 00:00:50.480
to make sure that the text was palatable to an English speaking audience.

00:00:50.620 --> 00:00:55.340
They've done a good job, for the most part, but in a game like Bloodborne

00:00:55.540 --> 00:01:00.960
even the slightest translation that's not literal can effect our interpretation.

00:01:01.760 --> 00:01:05.660
We found the best example of this in the Old Hunter's Bone description:

00:01:06.240 --> 00:01:08.940
"The bone of an old hunter whose name is lost.

00:01:08.940 --> 00:01:12.440
It is said that 'HE' was an apprentice to old Gehrman,

00:01:12.440 --> 00:01:18.540
and a practitioner of the art of Quickening, which is a technique particular to the First Hunters."

00:01:18.900 --> 00:01:22.820
What's weird is that in the Japanese description, there is no

00:01:22.980 --> 00:01:28.180
reference to this bone belonging to a man, so it could belong to a woman as well.

00:01:28.580 --> 00:01:31.860
And I can think of a more likely candidate, can't you?

00:01:32.580 --> 00:01:36.220
This bone lies upon the grave that transports us to the Hunter's Nightmare,

00:01:36.220 --> 00:01:40.800
which is a Nightmare full of old Hunters who possess this same art of Quickening

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:43.300
that the bone grants our hunter.

00:01:43.540 --> 00:01:48.360
So, sure, it could belong to any of the old Hunters, man or woman,

00:01:48.840 --> 00:01:52.620
but it just makes so much more sense if this belongs to Maria.

00:01:52.880 --> 00:01:55.600
She's linked to this grave very heavily.

00:01:55.600 --> 00:01:59.600
She was an apprentice to Gehrman's Workshop, she possesses the art of Quickening,

00:01:59.800 --> 00:02:04.140
Gehrman had an affection for Maria, he even created the doll in her image,

00:02:04.380 --> 00:02:11.360
the doll prays at this grave, and it's the only grave to lie just outside Gehrman's abandoned workshop.

00:02:11.720 --> 00:02:15.640
So, after looking at the Japanese description, I feel very confident in saying

00:02:15.640 --> 00:02:19.280
that Maria is the most likely candidate for this grave.

00:02:19.580 --> 00:02:22.400
Assuming this is right, we can take this assumption further.

00:02:22.720 --> 00:02:26.580
This grave exists in the waking world, meaning that Maria must have died

00:02:26.660 --> 00:02:28.900
before Gehrman's Hunter's Dream began.

00:02:29.100 --> 00:02:33.240
And this fact helps us put together a timeline and tell a story.

00:02:33.620 --> 00:02:37.780
Perhaps laying Maria to rest here inspired Gehrman's meeting

00:02:37.780 --> 00:02:41.780
with the Moon Presence and his subsequent escape into a dream

00:02:41.780 --> 00:02:45.140
where he created something in Maria's image.

00:02:45.340 --> 00:02:48.640
And it doesn't even matter if this is speculation because,

00:02:48.820 --> 00:02:53.740
even if you don't agree, my point is that this is a line of speculation that we couldn't

00:02:53.740 --> 00:02:59.180
even go down because the English translation said the grave belonged to a man.

00:02:59.560 --> 00:03:05.040
And that's what this video is about. It's about combing through significant item descriptions to make sure we

00:03:05.160 --> 00:03:12.160
haven't missed anything important, or to make sure we haven't been interpreting something wrong this whole time.

00:03:12.420 --> 00:03:18.020
So, if you're like me, and you care about documenting this stuff, then listen along.

00:03:18.380 --> 00:03:22.500
Also, let's get some love for the guy who made this video possible.

00:03:22.940 --> 00:03:25.700
He goes by the name Loremaster Nojah (check description for link).

00:03:26.040 --> 00:03:28.240
He's the one who hunted down the descriptions that

00:03:28.240 --> 00:03:31.500
I thought would most benefit us being translated.

00:03:31.720 --> 00:03:38.420
His initiative, his dedication, and his knowledge of the language is the basis of this video.

00:03:38.420 --> 00:03:42.920
Let's do something cool for the guy and help him get his YouTube channel off the ground.

00:03:43.260 --> 00:03:46.820
He's got these plans to create a play through of Souls games

00:03:46.820 --> 00:03:52.540
focusing on translations and the lore, so subscribe to him if that sounds interesting.

00:03:52.880 --> 00:03:54.940
Alright, so back to the translations.

00:03:55.180 --> 00:03:59.760
This gender discrepancy with the Old Hunter's Bone got me thinking,

00:03:59.760 --> 00:04:04.020
'What if other English Translations have misrepresented a gender?'

00:04:04.220 --> 00:04:08.160
I immediately thought of Alfred's dialogue where he says this:

00:04:08.640 --> 00:04:14.160
"Once, a scholar betrayed his fellows at Byrgenwerth and brought forbidden blood

00:04:14.160 --> 00:04:16.740
back with him to Cainhurst Castle.

00:04:17.160 --> 00:04:21.920
It was there that the first of the inhuman Vilebloods was born.

00:04:22.360 --> 00:04:28.680
The Vilebloods are fiendish creatures who threaten the purity of the Church's blood healing."

00:04:29.100 --> 00:04:35.440
Lo and behold, it turns out that this betrayer isn't necessarily a 'HE' either.

00:04:35.780 --> 00:04:40.120
In Japanese this betrayer is referred to with a gender-neutral expression.

00:04:40.360 --> 00:04:44.360
Which, obviously again,  opens him up to being a man or a woman.

00:04:45.300 --> 00:04:49.600
And who this betrayer is has always been a bit of a mystery.

00:04:49.980 --> 00:04:53.380
We don't even know if this betrayer is represented in-game.

00:04:53.700 --> 00:04:57.400
Before this video, most people thought that it was the Cainhurst Crow who

00:04:57.400 --> 00:05:02.760
appears in the Grand Cathedral since he uses the Old Hunter's Bone, which links him to the workshop,

00:05:03.040 --> 00:05:07.360
and he also dons the Cainhurst Mask which links him to Cainhurst.

00:05:07.620 --> 00:05:11.400
So it's possible that he betrayed the Byrgenwerth scholars and took

00:05:11.400 --> 00:05:15.540
that forbidden blood to Cainhurst to begin the Vileblood line.

00:05:15.840 --> 00:05:20.720
But now that the betrayer position is opened up to the female cast of Bloodborne,

00:05:21.100 --> 00:05:25.040
the only candidate I can think of is Maria, again, but I'm

00:05:25.040 --> 00:05:28.860
open to your ideas on this one since this is still speculation.

00:05:29.240 --> 00:05:34.540
Maria is related to the Vileblood Queen so she has links to Cainhurst and she clearly

00:05:34.540 --> 00:05:38.180
has links to the Byrgenwerth scholars because she was an apprentice to Gehrman,

00:05:38.180 --> 00:05:40.540
and she ended up in the Hunter's Nightmare.

00:05:40.540 --> 00:05:45.720
Plus, she resents what the Hunters did in the Fishing Hamlet, which could have inspired

00:05:45.820 --> 00:05:49.060
her to betray the Byrgenwerth scholars.

00:05:49.360 --> 00:05:54.420
But, again, there is nothing explicitly linking her to stealing Cainhurst's blood,

00:05:54.640 --> 00:05:57.560
so what I'm saying is kind of a long shot.

00:05:57.940 --> 00:06:04.460
Anyway, again, my point is that this long shot wouldn't even be possible unless we discovered this mistranslation.

00:06:04.780 --> 00:06:09.480
And it is worth pointing out that we don't know how  much contact the English translation team

00:06:09.540 --> 00:06:15.000
had to clarify questions of gender like this, so, bear that in mind.

00:06:15.280 --> 00:06:21.240
The betrayer is potentially referenced in the Japanese version of Laurence and Willem's cutscene.

00:06:24.980 --> 00:06:30.940
In Japanese the pronoun 'kimi' and the particle 'mo' can mean "you also".

00:06:34.420 --> 00:06:39.920
So we knew there was a split from Byrgenwerth and now we learn that they may have split

00:06:39.920 --> 00:06:42.440
before Laurence, not just after.

00:06:42.940 --> 00:06:55.180
What I also found interesting was these lines in Japanese which say (see above):

00:06:55.500 --> 00:07:01.900
The notion of "surpassing humanity (by the blood)" is largely missing from the English quote.

00:07:02.380 --> 00:07:08.400
Furthermore, the adage of Byrgenwerth says: "We urge you to fear the blood (as you proceed)",

00:07:08.820 --> 00:07:12.360
Where the English simply says "To fear the blood".

00:07:12.740 --> 00:07:18.360
Speaking of fear, the Harrowed Set explains a little bit more about why the general populace

00:07:18.360 --> 00:07:20.520
fear and hate the Hunters.

00:07:20.860 --> 00:07:24.940
In Japanese the Harrowed Set is actually "The Disguise Set".

00:07:25.220 --> 00:07:31.800
Worn by Hunters whose job it is to blend in with the populace and who have the power to act and kill

00:07:31.800 --> 00:07:34.880
anyone they suspect of being a beast.

00:07:35.280 --> 00:07:42.900
The English line:

00:07:43.360 --> 00:07:49.480
Becomes (translated from Japanese):

00:07:49.960 --> 00:07:56.020
The next line in English:

00:07:56.580 --> 00:08:01.680
Becomes (translated from Japanese):

00:08:01.980 --> 00:08:06.620
The final line in English:

00:08:07.220 --> 00:08:10.520
Becomes (translated from Japanese):

00:08:10.840 --> 00:08:15.640
And the implication here is that these Hunters had the Church-pardoned right

00:08:15.640 --> 00:08:19.700
to kill where ever they see fit, to investigate whomever they want.

00:08:20.020 --> 00:08:24.060
The English description posits them as the first line of defense against the outbreak,

00:08:24.060 --> 00:08:27.940
Hunters who sometimes see Beasthood where it doesn't exist,

00:08:28.220 --> 00:08:31.940
but the Japanese description suggests that these Hunters act with impunity,

00:08:31.940 --> 00:08:36.880
uncovering the secrets of the populace all under the pretense of beast hunting.

00:08:37.140 --> 00:08:44.240
And it does a lot to explain the paranoia of the populace, their fear of the church, and hatred of the Hunters.

00:08:44.560 --> 00:08:49.440
Another armor set title that wasn't replicated perfectly is the Tomb Prospector set.

00:08:49.720 --> 00:08:56.540
In Japanese, this name is actually a combination of the word 'tomb' and 'a thing that is rough or violent'

00:08:56.540 --> 00:08:58.940
or 'a thing that breaks open'.

00:08:59.120 --> 00:09:04.720
Nojah tells us that a direct translation would be "Tomb Break Opener", contrasting

00:09:04.780 --> 00:09:11.280
with "Tomb Prospector" which sounds really gentle and scholarly by comparison.

00:09:11.600 --> 00:09:16.460
We know from the way that the scholars treated the Fishing Hamlet that the scholars

00:09:16.460 --> 00:09:23.760
weren't particularly gentle with this ancient race of alien beings, and the Tomb Prospectors were no exception.

00:09:24.040 --> 00:09:28.200
In fact, they're downright rude in their naming of some Great Ones.

00:09:28.680 --> 00:09:33.580
'Rom, The Vacuous Spider' is actually 'Rom, The Stupid Spider'.

00:09:33.980 --> 00:09:38.360
The Japanese word 'hakuchi' means 'stupid or idiotic', and Nojah

00:09:38.500 --> 00:09:43.580
says that these are the words you use when you call someone a 'retard' or something.

00:09:43.660 --> 00:09:45.960
It carries that same social weight.

00:09:46.200 --> 00:09:48.240
I feel sorry for Rom now, damn.

00:09:48.500 --> 00:09:52.420
Rom is referenced by a few notes as somehow hiding rituals.

00:09:52.640 --> 00:09:59.400
When we kill him, in fact, Mensis and their ritual are revealed to us and we can enter their nightmare

00:09:59.520 --> 00:10:01.760
and supposedly interrupt it.

00:10:02.460 --> 00:10:07.320
Since Rom is within a great lake, it reminded me of the Arcane Lake rune.

00:10:07.740 --> 00:10:09.200
Here's its description:

00:10:09.200 --> 00:10:13.200
"Great volumes of water serve as a bulwark guarding sleep".

00:10:13.460 --> 00:10:19.260
The Japanese clarifies that 'guarding sleep' means 'preventing the sleep from being interrupted'.

00:10:19.580 --> 00:10:25.160
Which I found fitting because great bodies of water do prevent nightmares from being interrupted.

00:10:25.460 --> 00:10:31.360
Killing Rom in his giant lake allows us to interrupt the Mensis ritual, for example.

00:10:31.760 --> 00:10:35.320
The great body of water over the Nightmare of Yharnam also guards

00:10:35.320 --> 00:10:40.140
the source of the nightmare in the Fishing Hamlet preventing us from interrupting it.

00:10:40.540 --> 00:10:46.460
And speaking of Rom, did you ever notice that his corpse, or a corpse of a being like him,

00:10:46.740 --> 00:10:49.520
makes up the altar in front of Ebrietas?

00:10:49.820 --> 00:10:55.120
This is named the Altar of Despair in English, but in Japanese it's actually the

00:10:55.120 --> 00:10:58.900
Altar of Grief or Altar of Lamentations.

00:10:59.160 --> 00:11:05.780
And from the way Ebrietas is positioned when we first enter, not even aggroing until you hit her,

00:11:06.120 --> 00:11:12.100
we can surmise that this is an altar for her grief and her lamentations which, in my mind,

00:11:12.100 --> 00:11:16.100
sounds a little bit more personal than the Altar of Despair.

00:11:16.420 --> 00:11:22.580
I assume she's despairing because Rom, or this creature, has ascended without her

00:11:22.580 --> 00:11:27.960
since she is referenced as 'The Left Behind Great One'.

00:11:28.280 --> 00:11:34.820
Of all the information we do need, we need more information on the nature of the Great Ones.

00:11:35.080 --> 00:11:39.560
For that, we should look a little bit closer at the Umbilical Cords.

00:11:39.840 --> 00:11:44.060
It's very likely that these cords are needed to meet with the Great Ones.

00:11:44.380 --> 00:11:50.220
Worth noting is that Mensis's Cord says "it granted them audience with Mergo" in English,

00:11:50.520 --> 00:11:53.920
but in Japanese it clarifies that it didn't grant them an audience.

00:11:54.240 --> 00:11:58.000
Rather, it's described as (see above):

00:11:58.260 --> 00:12:03.740
Similarly, a note in the Lecture Building says, in English, the nameless Moon Presence

00:12:03.740 --> 00:12:08.180
was beckoned by Laurence and his associates; but in Japanese there is no mention

00:12:08.180 --> 00:12:14.160
of beckoning, and it simply says (see above).

00:12:14.620 --> 00:12:17.740
Finally, the Lower Loran Chalice description.

00:12:18.180 --> 00:12:23.500
The English says "there are trace remains of medical procedures in parts of Ailing Loran.

00:12:23.820 --> 00:12:27.760
Whether these were attempts to control the scourge of the beast is unknown."

00:12:28.080 --> 00:12:31.020
There is a significant deviation here in Japanese.

00:12:31.260 --> 00:12:38.180
The Japanese says "were these procedures countering the beast sickness, or, priming/causing them?".

00:12:38.540 --> 00:12:44.340
The expression used for 'priming' means literally (see above).

00:12:44.620 --> 00:12:48.960
To me, it sounds almost as if the Pthumerian's medical procedures mirrored the

00:12:48.960 --> 00:12:53.100
populace of Yharnam's, as they might have also discovered blood transfusion.

00:12:53.520 --> 00:12:58.580
The Japanese questions whether they were trying to control the plague outbreak with medicine,

00:12:58.580 --> 00:13:01.780
or causing it with medicine, like is done in Yharnam.

00:13:02.060 --> 00:13:03.960
So, yeah, interesting stuff.

00:13:04.220 --> 00:13:10.400
To finish up, let's rapid fire a few translations, cause they're really short and I don't need to go into too much depth.

00:13:10.760 --> 00:13:15.080
First, "The One Reborn" translates to "The Ones Reborn".

00:13:15.540 --> 00:13:20.080
Normally, Japanese doesn't pluralize, but the word to describe them means

00:13:20.240 --> 00:13:26.560
'to revive/reform/reorganize a group or institution that was defunct'.

00:13:27.000 --> 00:13:31.040
'Blood Echoes' are translated to being 'Dying Wishes of the Blood',

00:13:31.340 --> 00:13:37.340
which reminds me of the Heir Rune which posits that the heir is a Hunter who bears the

00:13:37.340 --> 00:13:39.520
echoing will of those before him.

00:13:39.760 --> 00:13:43.040
Furthermore, 'Insight' is actually 'Enlightenment'.

00:13:43.380 --> 00:13:45.700
'Frenzy' is actually 'Insanity'.

00:13:46.060 --> 00:13:48.600
'Bloodtinge' is actually 'Blood quality'

00:13:49.040 --> 00:13:55.860
In the Fishing Hamlet, 'The Wizened Child' is literally translated to 'The Infant Grown Old'.

00:13:56.280 --> 00:14:04.060
Maria's weapon, 'Rakuyo', is named 'Fallen Leaf' and is referred to in the game as a fairly famous blade.

00:14:04.440 --> 00:14:07.960
Next, the Doll knows that the Moon Presence is in the dream.

00:14:08.260 --> 00:14:12.360
In her dialogue where she says "O flora of the moon, of the dream...",

00:14:12.700 --> 00:14:16.960
it's clearer in Japanese that 'flora' is the name of the Moon Presence.

00:14:17.380 --> 00:14:20.940
It's curious that she knew it existed all along.

00:14:21.520 --> 00:14:29.620
When Micolash dies, in English he says "Now I'm waking up, I'll forget everything".

00:14:30.660 --> 00:14:33.460
But in Japanese, he's asking a question.

00:14:33.600 --> 00:14:37.100
He's questioning whether he'll wake up and remember anything.

00:14:37.560 --> 00:14:41.220
In Japanese, the Celestial Dial description has a double meaning.

00:14:41.580 --> 00:14:48.500
It says it 'will leak a secret to the user', which is another reference to the watery secret behind the clock.

00:14:49.140 --> 00:14:56.600
In the Corruption Rune, we learn that what Alfred calls 'Vilebloods' don't refer to themselves as 'Vilebloods'.

00:14:57.100 --> 00:15:01.700
Instead, they refer to themselves as 'The Blood Kin of Cainhurst'.

00:15:02.020 --> 00:15:06.480
The same term is used in Annalise's lines, making it clear that Vileblood

00:15:06.480 --> 00:15:10.500
is a slur, preferred by their Byrgenwerth rivals.

00:15:10.980 --> 00:15:15.300
Runesmith Caryll is described with more humble language in Japanese.

00:15:15.700 --> 00:15:17.780
He's called Copyist Caryll.

00:15:17.780 --> 00:15:24.460
His transcription of 'beast' in English says "it is one of the first runes, and one of the first to be forbidden".

00:15:24.900 --> 00:15:32.560
In Japanese it's said that "it is the first rune to be created and the first rune to be forbidden". No exceptions.

00:15:33.080 --> 00:15:35.760
And finally, we start at the beginning of the game.

00:15:36.080 --> 00:15:39.980
Remember that note that was left on the chair after your blood transfusion?

00:15:40.180 --> 00:15:42.900
"Seek Paleblood to transcend the hunt".

00:15:43.080 --> 00:15:49.280
In Japanese, it's actually "seek Paleblood to complete the hunt", and the Japanese reveals

00:15:49.280 --> 00:15:52.160
that you were the one that wrote this.

00:15:52.480 --> 00:15:58.540
It wasn't left for you by the man who did your transfusion; it was left there for you, by you.

00:15:59.140 --> 00:16:01.180
And thanks for watching, guys.

00:16:01.180 --> 00:16:04.020
I'm glad we could get a little bit more information out there.

00:16:04.260 --> 00:16:11.140
Special thanks to my Pateron supporters who make this stuff possible, and I'll see you all really soon.

